WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.260
Who doesn’t love dogs?

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:06.660
They’re friendly, energetic, and can be
beneficial to their owners’ happiness and

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:07.940
mental health.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:12.959
On top of all those positive qualities, most
dogs are fiercely loyal to their masters.

00:00:12.959 --> 00:00:17.990
You’ll often hear stories of dogs defending
their owners, or even staying by their side

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:22.840
through their very last days and even sticking
next to them beyond death.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:27.930
As sad as that thought might be to many dog
owners, it provides us the perfect context

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:29.180
for today’s topic.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:33.620
It’s about time that you met SCP-1111.

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:38.050
Sometimes also known by the nickname “The
White Dog”, this moniker actually refers

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:47.219
to one of the two halves of SCP-1111, namely
the former: SCP-1111-1, while its counterpart

00:00:47.219 --> 00:00:51.780
is simply known only as SCP-1111-2.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:57.879
As you may have already deduced, SCP-1111-1
is, or at least appears to be, a fairly common

00:00:57.879 --> 00:00:59.629
domesticated dog.

00:00:59.629 --> 00:01:03.969
Sporting white fur that gives it its nickname,
the White Dog is a cross between two different

00:01:03.969 --> 00:01:08.040
popular breeds, the German Shepherd and the
Labrador Retriever.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:13.990
However, upon closer inspection, this particular
pup is a far cry from one you might see fetching

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:16.750
sticks or chasing squirrels at the park.

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:19.990
For one, this dog never eats or drinks.

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:26.430
Under normal circumstances, that would be
worrying behavior in any dog, but in SCP-1111-1’s

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:31.289
case, it comes second to the fact that this
dog is partially see-through.

00:01:31.289 --> 00:01:37.020
Now that’s definitely not normal, in actual
fact this pooch is pretty far from ordinary.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:41.500
It seems to be at least semi-translucent,
not quite as much as we usually picture a

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:45.789
ghost or a hologram, but also not fully visible
like a living being.

00:01:45.789 --> 00:01:51.009
In fact, how clearly visible the White Dog
is can vary depending on how close it is to

00:01:51.009 --> 00:01:53.200
1111-2.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:57.549
Any further than five hundred meters away,
and the dog will gradually grow more and more

00:01:57.549 --> 00:02:00.509
transparent, but not fully invisible.

00:02:00.509 --> 00:02:05.479
But visibility isn’t the only thing that
shifts with 1111-1’s distance from its other

00:02:05.479 --> 00:02:08.849
half, the size of the dog also changes.

00:02:08.849 --> 00:02:15.209
It remains standing at 150 centimeters when
directly beneath 1111-2 and gradually gets

00:02:15.209 --> 00:02:20.060
smaller the further and further away from
1111-2 it gets.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:23.360
Finally, there’s its eyes.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:29.320
SCP-1111-1 possesses a distinct pair of glowing
red eyes, the brightness and intensity of

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:33.340
which increase the closer it is to 1111-2.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:38.290
So let’s recap: so far we have a strange
white dog with glowing eyes, that changes

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:43.260
size and becomes more or less visible the
further it gets from a secondary element.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:49.489
But, if the White Dog is SCP-1111-1, then
what forms this second part of SCP-1111?

00:02:49.489 --> 00:02:54.290
Well, if you were to look close enough at
the white dog, you’d notice the red collar

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:56.440
that it wears around its neck.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:01.980
And hanging from that collar is a tag, on
which is printed one single word: “Loyal.”

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:05.569
It’s certainly a fitting word to describe
1111-1.

00:03:05.569 --> 00:03:06.939
Why?

00:03:06.939 --> 00:03:14.940
Because SCP-1111-2 is presumably the dog’s
master - or rather, its master’s dead body.

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:20.460
Dressed in an old, worn business suit and
formal dress shoes, SCP-1111-2 appears to

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:23.330
be a deceased male of indeterminate age.

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:27.920
The precise identity of this man has proven
next to impossible for Foundation researchers

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:29.090
to determine.

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:33.760
The condition of his suit and shoes have deteriorated
so much that it has been difficult to even

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:38.370
identify the original company that produced
the clothing worn by the corpse.

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:39.950
As for his cause of death?

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:46.250
Well, that unfortunately seems all too obvious,
given that the 1111-2 body always appears

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:50.780
the same way: hanging from a tree with a noose
around his neck.

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:56.629
Foundation staff observing the two parts that
make up SCP-1111 have noted that 1111-2 will

00:03:56.629 --> 00:04:00.350
occasionally make quick, violent twitching
movements.

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:04.780
These random jerks and spasms of the corpse
are consistent with those exhibited by a person

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:09.600
who is dying from asphyxiation, and often
researchers have heard the body making desperate

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.280
gasps for air.

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:16.690
The closer his white furred canine counterpart
is, the more frequent and violent these motions

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:18.190
and sounds will become.

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:24.770
It’s almost as if SCP-1111-2 has somehow
been trapped on the very brink of death, reliving

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:31.240
those final moments over and over again, all
while guarded by his loyal White Dog.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:35.590
If left alone and not interfered with, the
White Dog will lie down just beneath where

00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:37.510
its master’s body is hanging.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:42.820
The dog never sleeps, nor does it require
any food or water, and does not even seem

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:44.030
to breathe.

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:49.780
And as long as Foundation research staff keep
their distance, both parts of SCP-1111 seem

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:52.360
content to remain in a docile state.

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:56.970
To keep them contained, the SCP Foundation
has established a two kilometer safe zone

00:04:56.970 --> 00:05:02.400
around SCP-1111, keeping them monitored through
cameras attached to weather balloons.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:07.120
The restricted enclosure is, according to
a public cover story, a weather monitoring

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:09.419
station, hence the balloons.

00:05:09.419 --> 00:05:14.889
No member of Foundation staff is permitted
anywhere within a kilometer of SCP-1111, unless

00:05:14.889 --> 00:05:18.669
they are given express permission from a superior
member of the Foundation.

00:05:18.669 --> 00:05:24.550
Should SCP-1111-1 ever strays away from the
tree where its master hangs though, then the

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:29.710
area must be evacuated of all personnel until
the dog returns to its normal position.

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:35.370
However, Foundation staff are urged to be
wary when approaching SCP-1111, because the

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:39.419
White Dog may well be more ferociously loyal
than any pet.

00:05:39.419 --> 00:05:41.290
Emphasis on ferocious.

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:47.330
The moment that 1111-1 becomes aware of anything
coming towards itself and its owner’s body,

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:50.090
the dog will become viciously hostile.

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:54.560
Regardless of the person or object coming
towards it, the semi-corporeal canine will

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:56.710
attempt to attack and destroy the intruder.

00:05:56.710 --> 00:06:01.660
In this state, the White Dog exhibits even
more dramatic physiological differences from

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:03.870
a normal domesticated dog.

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:08.229
Video footage recorded by the SCP Foundation
shows that the dog is capable of reaching

00:06:08.229 --> 00:06:13.470
incredible speeds of up to sixty kilometers
per hour, which is of course considerably

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.840
faster than an average canine.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:20.330
The White Dog can also reach a height of six
meters when jumping up into the air, and has

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:24.349
teeth and a bite strength powerful enough
to tear through armor plating composed of

00:06:24.349 --> 00:06:27.240
fifteen-millimeter-thick titanium.

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:32.150
Given the entity’s speed, aggression, and
translucent qualities, any attempts by the

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:37.580
SCP Foundation to neutralize the White Dog,
or even capture it for closer examination,

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:41.650
have ended the same grisly way for the staff
members who tried.

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:45.470
The creature’s fierce loyalty defending
its owner’s body also makes it incredibly

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:51.410
difficult for Foundation staff to even get
close enough to SCP-1111-2 to properly study

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:52.750
the remains.

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:57.890
As we said before, that “loyal” tag around
the dog’s neck is certainly an accurate

00:06:57.890 --> 00:06:59.129
description.

00:06:59.129 --> 00:07:04.220
On a date which has been redacted from its
file, an incident occurred involving SCP-1111

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:07.830
and a team that consisted of a number of Foundation
agents.

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:12.449
This team had been ordered to neutralize the
White Dog, and transport the anomalous animal

00:07:12.449 --> 00:07:14.599
to a containment facility.

00:07:14.599 --> 00:07:18.440
Attempting to evade the creature’s direct
line of sight, the agents approached the hanging

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:25.509
body of SCP-1111-2 from the North - the opposite
direction to the way the dog was facing.

00:07:25.509 --> 00:07:29.699
Possessing a sense of hearing and smell far
beyond that of a human being, the White Dog

00:07:29.699 --> 00:07:33.039
was able to quickly detect the agents approaching
its master.

00:07:33.039 --> 00:07:37.199
When the team got within three hundred meters
of the tree where the body was hanging, the

00:07:37.199 --> 00:07:41.750
canine set upon them, tearing at clothing
and shredding protective armor with its teeth

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:45.159
in order to get to the agents’ soft flesh
underneath.

00:07:45.159 --> 00:07:48.620
One of these agents fled, running as fast
as they could from the area.

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:53.800
But, of course, this was a futile move, as
the White Dog quickly noticed and began to

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:57.479
pursue the Foundation agent with its super
powered speed.

00:07:57.479 --> 00:08:03.889
As it chased them, surveillance cameras recorded
SCP-1111-1 decreasing in size, becoming harder

00:08:03.889 --> 00:08:07.099
to see with the naked eye the further it ran
from the tree.

00:08:07.099 --> 00:08:09.780
The dog’s speed began to decline too.

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:14.130
The further the dog got from the tree with
noose, the less the body hanging from it seemed

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:15.879
to be spasming too.

00:08:15.879 --> 00:08:21.289
When the White Dog had reached 900 meters
from SCP-1111-2, the corpse was seen to stop

00:08:21.289 --> 00:08:27.419
moving entirely, frozen and stiff, as one
would normally expect a deceased body to be.

00:08:27.419 --> 00:08:34.710
Realizing how far away it was from its master,
SCP-1111-1 froze, appearing unsure for a moment.

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:39.130
It turned to look towards the body of its
master, perhaps sensing that the random jerks

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:41.260
and post-mortem movements had stopped.

00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:45.730
At this point, the dog howled and sprinted
back towards the tree, causing the corpse

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:48.420
of its owner to begin twitching yet again.

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:52.940
Footage of this incident showed that the White
Dog was impervious to conventional weapons,

00:08:52.940 --> 00:08:58.150
and any rounds fired at the canine by Foundation
agents merely passed through its ghostly body.

00:08:58.150 --> 00:09:03.480
However, its claws and teeth were very much
solid, and it was able to slaughter almost

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:09.090
all the agents, save for the one who fled,
who ended up to be the sole survivor of the

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:10.090
encounter.

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:13.780
Following this disastrous mission, the O5
Council issued an order that, in order to

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:18.780
protect the lives of Foundation personnel,
only remote controlled drones and expendable

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:22.950
D-class personnel would be permitted anywhere
near SCP-1111.

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:27.480
Shortly after the previous incident, a group
of D-class were sent into the area around

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:33.100
the tree where SCP-1111-2 was hanging, this
time approaching from multiple directions

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:34.160
at once.

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:39.100
But this only led to the same results, as
the White Dog began to quickly move between

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:43.220
each of the D-classes, killing them one after
another.

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:49.080
Only one, D-83011, was able to make it close
enough to the corpse to make any noteworthy

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:50.500
observations.

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:56.560
As they approached, the hanging corpse of
SCP-1111-2 seemed to slow its jerks and twitches,

00:09:56.560 --> 00:10:01.660
and the body did something that had never
been seen before, it opened its eyes.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:06.360
It raised its arms towards the approaching
D-class in what looked like a welcoming hug,

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:11.970
only for D-83011 to be torn to shreds by the
White Dog moments after.

00:10:11.970 --> 00:10:16.960
Cameras nearby picked up more previously unseen
movement, namely the owner’s mouth moving,

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:21.060
almost as if he was saying the words “no,
down boy.”

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:25.780
But soon after, the corpse fell limp again
and resumed its normal twitches.

00:10:25.780 --> 00:10:30.000
Following this, the Foundation have theorized
that the White Dog could possibly be contained

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:33.220
by somehow removing its master’s body from
the area.

00:10:33.220 --> 00:10:40.100
Some staff have also noted that SCP-1111 shares
certain traits with SCP-023, a similar anomalous

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:43.160
creature also referred to as The Black Shuck.

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:48.380
Much like the White Dog, the Shuck also possesses
a ghostly canine form and appears to be the

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:53.660
same large, dog-like creature that is referenced
in ancient folklore from throughout the British

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:54.660
Isles.

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:59.340
According to legends, the Shuck appears to
travelers at crossroads, serving as an omen

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:05.710
of bad luck, impending disaster, and is even
thought to be one of the hounds of Hell itself.

00:11:05.710 --> 00:11:12.840
SCP-023, like SCP-1111, also has anomalous
abilities that focus on geographic space.

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:17.430
In the Black Shuck’s case, anyone it detects
approaching it will die or lose a member of

00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:19.710
their family within a year.

00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:26.670
Researchers working for the Foundation believed
that SCP-023 and SCP-1111-1 could be related,

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:32.450
or even instances of the same phenomenon,
a sort of dog yin and yang, but since they

00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:37.900
have still, as of yet, been unable to capture
the White Dog, it has been impossible to verify

00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:38.900
this.

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:41.400
The SCP Foundation will no doubt keep trying
though.

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:45.340
While testing may have been suspended for
the time being, they always know where to

00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:52.850
find SCP-1111 - beneath its master’s hanged
body, guarding it, for all eternity.

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:59.650
Now go check out “SCP-1913 Deadly Monster
Squad - The Furies” and “SCP-2845 - Alien

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:04.970
God Crash Lands on Earth - THE DEER” for
more animal SCPs you have to see to believe!

